FFDDTT CCOONNFFIIGGUURRAATTIIOONN
     On an fdt(4) based system, the mmxx2255ll device is defined as a slave device
     subnode of the SPI bus controller node.  All properties documented in the
     _s_p_i_b_u_s_._t_x_t bindings document can be used with the mmxx2255ll device.  The most
     commonly-used ones are documented below.

     The following properties are required in the mmxx2255ll device subnode:

     _c_o_m_p_a_t_i_b_l_e
             Must be the string "jedec,spi-nor".

     _r_e_g     Chip select address of device.

     _s_p_i_-_m_a_x_-_f_r_e_q_u_e_n_c_y
             The maximum bus frequency to use when communicating with this
             slave device.  Actual bus speed may be lower, depending on the
             capabilities of the SPI bus controller hardware.

     The following properties are optional for the mmxx2255ll device subnode:

     _s_p_i_-_c_p_h_a
             Empty property indicating the slave device requires shifted clock
             phase (CPHA) mode.

     _s_p_i_-_c_p_o_l
             Empty property indicating the slave device requires inverse clock
             polarity (CPOL) mode.

     _s_p_i_-_c_s_-_h_i_g_h
             Empty property indicating the slave device requires chip select
             active high.

